OL,3,GNEWSAWarning to dog owners after pet
OL,4,Arescued from sea
OL,5,
OL,6,FCoastguards have urged dog owners never
OL,7,Fto attempt to rescue their pets from
OL,8,Fthe sea themselves after a person got
OL,9,Fstuck in mud while trying to retrieve
OL,10,Ftheir animal.
OL,12,FThe dog was reported to have run away
OL,13,Ffrom its owners and was struggling
OL,14,Faround 980ft (300m) offshore at
OL,15,FThurstaston Beach, Wirral, when it was
OL,16,Fsaved by the Wirral Coastguard Rescue
OL,17,FTeam earlier.
OL,19,FHM Coastguard Officer Steve Allen said
OL,20,Fone of the owners had attempted to
OL,21,Frescue it but became stuck knee-deep in
OL,22,Fmud with the tide coming in.
OL,23,APub: 15-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,406,400,260,160,0,100
